# setup-vlhe-menu - the SHAPE of setup-vlhe's menus: which exist,
#                   what each holds, in what order, nested how deep.
#
# Copyright (c) 2026 Thomas Tranter
# SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
#
# Part of VLHE. See LICENSE for the full license text.
#
# READ BY setup-vlhe AT START. This file is the user's: move a line
# and the item moves, add a `menu' block and it is nested, and the
# engine never knows the shape. The words are in setup-vlhe-strings;
# the settings themselves (their keys, types, defaults, bounds and
# choices) are the engine's and cannot be added here.
#
# TWO KINDS OF LINE, words separated by spaces, `#' to end of line a
# comment, blank lines ignored:
#
#   menu  NAME               declares a menu. Its title is
#                            STR_MENU_NAME in setup-vlhe-strings; the
#                            engine starts in `main', which must exist
#   item  MENU  KEY          a setting, by its key, as the next row of
#                            MENU. Its name is STR_KEY, its help
#                            STR_KEY_HELP
#   item  MENU  NAME  submenu
#                            a row of MENU that opens menu NAME
#
# Rows are numbered in the order the lines appear. Every menu offers
# s (save) and q (quit); a submenu offers b (back) as well.
#
# A KEY THAT IS NOT A SETTING, a submenu that is not a `menu', or a
# `main' that is missing is refused at start with the line number.
# A setting this file does not mention is simply not offered - it
# keeps its default (or what the existing config says) and is still
# written, which is the "partial is valid" rule of design/33.
#
# THE LAYOUT IS THE USER'S, APPROVED 2026-10-05 (design/33 section 3i,
# "THE APPROVED LAYOUT"): seven rows on the main menu - an Enable and a
# Settings submenu for each module, then Debugging - where it was one
# flat list of 21 that did not fit a 25-line console. The Enables are
# the three LoadAtBoot keys; their yes/no screens say what that means.

menu main
item main LoadAtBoot
item main sound submenu
item main MidiLoadAtBoot
item main midi submenu
item main CdLoadAtBoot
item main cd submenu
item main debug submenu
item main advanced submenu

menu sound
item sound CardDevice
item sound ProgramsUse
item sound MidiChannel
item sound ReleaseOnIdle
item sound MixRate
item sound Limiter
item sound Attenuation
item sound SaveMixerLevels
item sound SaveProgramLevels

menu midi
item midi DefaultFont0
item midi DefaultFont1
item midi Voices
item midi AutoVoices
item midi Gain
item midi Law
item midi Filter
item midi Rate
item midi Reverb
item midi Chorus
item midi ModEnv

menu cd
